Pengfei Cheng received his B.S. degree from Hubei University in 2015 and his M.Sc. degree from South China Normal University in 2019. He finished his public defense of Ph.D. degree at the Technische Universität Ilmenau in 2023. He is now a postdoctoral fellow in under the supervision of Prof. Dangyuan Lei. His research interests focus on the plasmonic local heating and radiative cooling.
Yidan An received his B.S. degree from Lanzhou University of Technology in 2016 and his M.Sc. & Ph.D. degrees from Soochow University in 2021. Now, he is a postdoc fellow under the supervision of Prof. Hin-Lap Yip. His research interests focus on the field of high-efficiency perovskite solar cells and radiative cooling.
Alex K.-Y. Jen is the Lee Shau Kee Chair Professor of Materials Science and Chair Professor of Chemistry and Materials Science of the City University of Hong Kong. He received his B.S. from the National Tsing Hua University in Taiwan and Ph.D. from the University of Pennsylvania in USA. Before arriving CityU, he served as the Boeing-Johnson Chair Professor and Chair of the Department of Materials Science & Engineering at the University of Washington, Seattle. His interdisciplinary research covers organic/hybrid functional materials and devices for photonics, energy, sensors, and nanomedicine.
Dangyuan Lei is a professor at the Department of Materials Science and Engineering in the City University of Hong Kong and Provost's visiting professor of physics at Imperial College London. He received his B.Sc., M.Phil. and Ph.D. degrees all in physics from Northwest University, The Chinese University of Hong Kong and Imperial College London in 2005, 2007 and 2011, respectively. His research interest focuses on plasmonic nanophotonics, nonlinear optics, low-dimensional quantum materials, and ultrafast optical spectroscopy, with particular interest in cavity-enhanced light–matter interactions at the nanoscale and device applications in miniaturized optoelectronics, optical sensing, imaging, energy conversion and saving.
